// Title: Disk Image Mounting Via Hdiutil - MacOS
// Sigma ID: bf241472-f014-4f01-a869-96f99330ca8c
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Omar Khaled (@beacon_exe)
// Date: 2024-08-10 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: initial-access, collection, T1566.001, T1560.001
// Description: Detects the execution of the hdiutil utility in order to mount disk images.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of hdiutil by administrators and users.
// References:
//   - https://www.loobins.io/binaries/hdiutil/
//   - https://www.sentinelone.com/blog/from-the-front-linesunsigned-macos-orat-malware-gambles-for-the-win/
//   - https://ss64.com/mac/hdiutil.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_hdiutil_mount.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/hdiutil" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "attach " or ProcessCommandLine contains "mount ")
